--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -33,3 +33,18 @@ applyPatch({ foo: ["bar"] }, [
   { op: "test", path: "/foo/0", value: "bar" },
 ]); // { foo: ["bar", "baz"] }
 ```
+
+## JSON Merge Patch
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` (from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Merge Patch, as [RFC 7386](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386),
+to a JSON document. It is the format for partial updates: an object patch merges into the target, a member set to `null` removes
+that member, and any other patch, such as an array or a scalar, replaces the target as a whole. A patch cannot set a member to `null`;
+use JSON Patch when that is needed.
+
+It returns the merged document as a new value and never modifies its inputs. It throws a `JsonMergePatchError` when the target or
+the patch is not a JSON value.
+
+```ts
+applyMergePatch({ title: "Draft", tags: ["a"], owner: "ana" }, { title: "Final", owner: null });
+// { title: "Final", tags: ["a"] }
+```
